### Start the API with npm start. Replace the token and item ID after login/creation.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@token = REPLACE_WITH_LOGIN_TOKEN
@itemId = REPLACE_WITH_CREATED_ITEM_ID

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### OpenAPI specification
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi.json

### Register (201). Choose another email if this account already exists.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sam",
  "email": "sam@example.com",
  "password": "a-long-demo-password"
}

### Login (200). Copy token from the response into @token above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sam@example.com",
  "password": "a-long-demo-password"
}

### Current account
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Report a lost item (201). Copy item.id into @itemId above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "lost",
  "title": "Blue backpack",
  "description": "A blue backpack with a small red keyring.",
  "category": "Bags",
  "location": "Central library",
  "eventDate": "2026-01-01"
}

### Report a found item
POST {{baseUrl}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "found",
  "title": "Silver keys",
  "description": "Two silver keys on a plain black keyring.",
  "category": "Keys",
  "location": "Main entrance",
  "eventDate": "2026-01-01"
}

### Public item details
GET {{baseUrl}}/items/{{itemId}}

### Search with combined filters and pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/items?q=backpack&type=lost&status=open&category=bag&location=library&from=2026-01-01&to=2026-01-01&page=1&limit=10

### Only my reports
GET {{baseUrl}}/items?mine=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Edit your open report
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "location": "Central library, reading room"
}

### Mark recovered (200). Repeating this preserves both timestamps.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/items/{{itemId}}/recover
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Recovered reports remain searchable
GET {{baseUrl}}/items?status=recovered

### Editing a recovered report returns 409 ITEM_RECOVERED.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated backpack"
}

### Log out (204). The token is immediately revoked.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Revoked tokens return 401.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
